story_text.value:
Managing data transformation (e.g. dbt) projects at scale can be challenging: DAG violations, that one model that grew to 2K lines, duplicated logic.<p>Inspired by the book 'Building Evolutionary Architectures' I built tff to help data transformation projects evolve in a desired direction. It comes with a github bot that you can plugin to your CI pipeline.<p>It aims to let transformation projects evolve in the desired direction by:
* ensuring layer boundary integrity;
* detect duplicate CTE logic;
* catch violations locally and in CI<p>Core concepts: rules apply to models; checks apply to architecture and DAG checks.<p>Curious to read what you think. What can be improved? What's missing?

